Bits.Description:
Read and write arbitration mode. Selects which direction the controller serves first when a read and a write are both waiting for the HyperBus.

Usage: program it before enable or while idle. A read that overlaps the bytes of an older pending write always waits for that write, whatever the mode. After 8 consecutive segments of the preferred direction one segment of the other direction is served.

Values:
0x0 round robin (reset value);
0x1 read priority;
0x2 write priority;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: do not write 0x3.

Waited-for event. The step that the controller was waiting for when the time ran out.

Usage: read-only; valid only while valid = 1; together with cmd it tells whether the device or the AXI side was late.

Values:
0x0 none;
0x1 RWDS level in the command phase;
0x2 first read data strobe edge after the latency;
0x3 next read data strobe edge in a burst;
0x4 capture FIFO data;
0x5 to 0xF reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Command in progress. The kind of command that the controller was executing.

Usage: read-only; valid only while valid = 1.

Values:
0x0 none;
0x1 start-up register write;
0x2 start-up ID0 read;
0x3 memory read;
0x4 memory write;
0x5 device register read;
0x6 device register write;
0x7 to 0xF reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Wrapped burst group size. Value written into CR0[1:0]; an AXI WRAP burst of the same byte length is sent as one wrapped HyperBus burst, others are split into two linear bursts.

Usage: program it while hr_ctrl.en = 0; choose the cache line size of the system for critical-word-first reads.

Values:
0x0 128 bytes;
0x1 64 bytes;
0x2 16 bytes;
0x3 32 bytes (reset value).

Unit: code.

Limits: none.

